NAME
     setfattr - write extended attributes

SYNOPSIS
     setfattr -n NAME [-v VALUE | -f FILE] FILE...
     setfattr -x NAME FILE...

DESCRIPTION
     setfattr sets an extended attribute on each FILE, from a value on
     the command line or the contents of a file, or removes one.

OPTIONS
     -n NAME    the attribute
     -v VALUE   its value
     -f FILE    take the value from FILE
     -x NAME    remove the attribute

SEE ALSO
     getfattr(1)
